course: dictionary
lesson: 15573
title: Sustenance: food and strength
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sustenance is a formal word for food and drink. It is what keeps a living thing alive and strong. «The hikers packed dried fruit and water for sustenance.» The hikers needed food and drink to keep going, so sustenance means food and drink here.
explain: Sustenance can also mean something that gives you strength inside, like comfort, hope or faith. «Her letters gave him sustenance during the long, lonely winter.» Nobody ate anything. The letters kept him going, so sustenance here means support that strengthens a person.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Ask: is the sentence about eating, drinking or staying alive? Or is it about feeling strong, brave or comforted? Then swap in "food and drink" or "support" to see which one fits.
fact: Sustenance is a noun. It is formal, so you will meet it more in old books, history and the Bible than in everyday chat.
fact: Sustenance means food and drink that keeps a person, animal or plant alive and strong.
fact: Sustenance can also mean anything that supports or strengthens someone, like comfort, hope or faith.
fact: In science, sustenance links to food chains and the nutrients that living things need.
fact: Phrases to know: "means of sustenance" (a way of getting the food you need to live), "spiritual sustenance" (faith or prayer that feeds the spirit), "for sustenance".
exercise: «The old sailors ran low on sustenance.» Find and copy the word that means food and drink. | sailors | *sustenance | low | old
exercise: «The travellers had no sustenance for days.» What does sustenance mean here? | *Food and drink to keep them alive | A new pair of boots | A map of the road | A warm bed for the night
exercise: «Her letters gave him sustenance when he was lonely.» What does sustenance mean here? | A stamp on an envelope | Bright lights in the window | *Comfort and hope that kept him going | Silence and rest
test: Which word could replace sustenance in «The soup gave the hungry walkers sustenance»? | *Nourishment | Silence | Hurry | Colour
test: In «Her kind words were sustenance to his weary heart», what does sustenance mean? | Heavy rain | A sweet snack | *Support that strengthens him | A bad cold
exam: Which is the best way to work out the meaning of sustenance in a new sentence? | *Swap in a simple meaning like food or support and see if the sentence still makes sense | Decide it must be a colour | Skip the whole text and never come back to it | Guess from the first letter only
